   "subject": "Categorical Variables.",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi all.<br>Is there a way of obtaining odds ratios for specific \r\ncategories and not just the whole variable. An example is say a variable\r\n education level with categories( Primary, secondary and tertiary level), is there a way of maybe specifying say primary level as the reference variable<br>and getting the odds ratios of secondary and tertiary level in reference to primary level. <br></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "yJhiS2sfYh0J",
   "from": "Okango Elphas",
   "author": "e7c1c94188a28a69",
   "date": "2015-05-11T08:07:33Z",
   "subject": "Re: Categorical Variables.",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"border-collapse:separate;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:13px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:15px;text-align:-webkit-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:pre-wrap;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(225,226,229)\"><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:10pt!important;outline-style:none;outline-width:initial;outline-color:initial;border-top-style:none;border-right-style:none;border-bottom-style:none;border-left-style:none;border-width:initial;border-color:initial;white-space:pre-wrap!important;word-break:break-all;margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;line-height:1.2\">Dear H Rue.<br>The variable education level has 3 categories: Primary, secondary, Tertiary. The problem is how to set primary level e.t.c as the reference category so that instead of having the result as below where only the (0.025quant 0.5quant 0.975quant) for the categorical variable: education level is given, <br>Table 1<br>Fixed effects:\r\n                       mean     sd 0.025quant 0.5quant 0.975quant    mode kld\r\n(Intercept)         -1.8422 0.7013    -3.2502  -1.8315    -0.4942 -1.8099   0\r\neducationlevel      -0.2020 0.0733    -0.3475  -0.2015    -0.0594 -0.2005   0\r\nage_first_sex       -0.3453 0.0796    -0.5008  -0.3455    -0.1885 -0.3460   0\r\nperceived_Risk       0.0256 0.0622    -0.0961   0.0255     0.1480  0.0252   0\r\npartners_last_1yr    0.3775 0.2324    -0.0941   0.3829     0.8191  0.3938   0\r\nUrban                0.4062 0.1746     0.0591   0.4075     0.7453  0.4103   0\r\nFreq_of_travel_away  0.0604 0.0593    -0.0576   0.0609     0.1756  0.0618   0\r\nMaritalStatusX       0.2094 0.0429     0.1247   0.2095     0.2930  0.2099   0\r\nSTI                 -0.5421 0.2772    -1.0652  -0.5498     0.0249 -0.5656   0\r\n</pre></span><br>we would have the 0.025quant 0.5quant 0.975quant for each level say:<br>Table 2<br>\r\n\r\n<table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;border:none\" border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\">\r\n <tbody><tr>\r\n  <td style=\"width:144.1pt;border:none;border-top:solid black 1.0pt;background:silver;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt\" valign=\"top\" width=\"192\">\r\n  <p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;color:black\">Variable</span></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n  <td style=\"width:105.65pt;border:none;border-top:solid black 1.0pt;background:silver;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt\" valign=\"top\" width=\"141\">\r\n  <p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;color:black\">0.25quant</span></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n  <td style=\"width:120.8pt;border:none;border-top:solid black 1.0pt;background:silver;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt\" valign=\"top\" width=\"161\">\r\n  <p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;color:black\">0.5quant</span></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n  <td style=\"width:108.25pt;border:none;border-top:solid black 1.0pt;background:silver;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt\" valign=\"top\" width=\"144\">\r\n  <p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;color:black\">0.75quant</span></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr>\r\n  <td style=\"width:144.1pt;border:none;background:silver;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt\" valign=\"top\" width=\"192\">\r\n  <p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;color:black\">Education(ref primary)</span></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n  <td style=\"width:105.65pt;border:none;background:silver;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt\" valign=\"top\" width=\"141\">\r\n  <p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;color:black\">1</span></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n  <td style=\"width:120.8pt;border:none;background:silver;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt\" valign=\"top\" width=\"161\">\r\n  <p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;color:black\">1</span></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n  <td style=\"width:108.25pt;border:none;background:silver;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt\" valign=\"top\" width=\"144\">\r\n  <p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;color:black\"> </span></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr>\r\n  <td style=\"width:144.1pt;border:none;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt\" valign=\"top\" width=\"192\">\r\n  <p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;color:black\">Secondary level<br></span></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n  <td style=\"width:105.65pt;border:none;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt\" valign=\"top\" width=\"141\">\r\n  <p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;color:black\">2.34<br></span></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n  <td style=\"width:120.8pt;border:none;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt\" valign=\"top\" width=\"161\">\r\n  <p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;color:black\">3.32</span></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n  <td style=\"width:108.25pt;border:none;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt\" valign=\"top\" width=\"144\">\r\n  <p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;color:black\">7.453</span></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr>\r\n  <td style=\"width:144.1pt;border:none;border-bottom:solid black 1.0pt;background:silver;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt\" valign=\"top\" width=\"192\">\r\n  <p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;color:black\">Tetiary level<br></span></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n  <td style=\"width:105.65pt;border:none;border-bottom:solid black 1.0pt;background:silver;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt\" valign=\"top\" width=\"141\">\r\n  <p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;color:black\">1.22<br></span></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n  <td style=\"width:120.8pt;border:none;border-bottom:solid black 1.0pt;background:silver;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt\" valign=\"top\" width=\"161\">\r\n  <p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;color:black\">2.12<br></span></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n  <td style=\"width:108.25pt;border:none;border-bottom:solid black 1.0pt;background:silver;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt\" valign=\"top\" width=\"144\">\r\n  <p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;color:black\">3.632</span></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n </tr>\r\n</tbody></table>\r\n\r\n so that we can be able to report the odds with reference to the primary level. say from table 2 the odds of an individual with secondary education is 3.32 more likely than that with primary education.</div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><br><br>On Monday, 11 May 2015 09:30:14 UTC+2, Okango Elphas  wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi all.<br>Is there a way of obtaining odds ratios for specific \r\ncategories and not just the whole variable. An example is say a variable\r\n education level with categories( Primary, secondary and tertiary level), is there a way of maybe specifying say primary level as the reference variable<br>and getting the odds ratios of secondary and tertiary level in reference to primary level. <br></div></blockquote></div>"
